    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5f7a6ec_943248e2",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 152,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T13:49:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SkTaskGroup (and nested SkThreadPool) both have their own internal thread safety controls. The spin lock here is to guard against the PipelineManager\u0027s own modification of the pointer. Mainly the modification of it in PipelineManager::shutDown.",
      "parentUuid": "a4d0fbd8_890a8f99",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "44606ea8fd183f97c4d30feded432572fb0ddf7a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44dbb9c5_0d50010b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 285,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-05T21:54:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s probably a good idea to put a comment here why the mutex is still needed because of its use with std::condition_variable. My understanding of that is that without a mutex, the single atomic fCompleted still allows the following scenario to have:\n\nMain thread: checks task-\u003efCompleted and see\u0027s its false, so no early return.\nPrecompile thread: marks task-\u003efCompleted true\nPrecompile thread: signals condition variable\nMain thread: waits on condition variable but the signal already occurred so we\u0027re stuck waiting.\n\nIt\u0027s okay (and hence why lock.unlock() before signal() is fine above) for the condition variable to be signaled outside of the mutex, but we require the mutex to group the check and the wait into one exclusive block of code vs. the code that modifies the check.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 277,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 285,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "44606ea8fd183f97c4d30feded432572fb0ddf7a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bc78a38_03ffaaa8",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 285,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T13:49:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve added the comment and, yeah, you\u0027re correct. Here is the relevant stackoverflow link:\n \nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/38147825/shared-atomic-variable-is-not-properly-published-if-it-is-not-modified-under-mut",
      "parentUuid": "44dbb9c5_0d50010b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 277,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 285,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "44606ea8fd183f97c4d30feded432572fb0ddf7a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8c83c5f_ad36a4d9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-05T21:54:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should document that this is a choice to limit the number of mutexes/semaphores etc. that are floating around for synchronizing access to the pipelines. Since the Context thread is the only place that resolves handles, we only ever have to wait on at most one pipeline at a time and no other thread will need to block on waiting for a different pipeline.  This means we don\u0027t need to add a condition_variable to every PipelineCreationTask for instance.\n\nThat said, I don\u0027t love having to mix thread safety primitives and I wonder if it\u0027s worth doing a bit of work to add a version of SkConditionVariable or SkGate/Latch similar to how we\u0027ve added SkSemaphore and SkMutex.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "44606ea8fd183f97c4d30feded432572fb0ddf7a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
